senses.gloss:
(I)--(हयशीर्ष)--a manifestation of Hari worshipped as such by भद्रश्रवस्: Half-man and half- horse: got back to ब्रह्मा the Vedas seized by Asura Madhu of रसातल;
1: भा. V. १८. 1-6; XI. 4. १७.
the form of विष्णु who appeared before Agastya [page३-742+ ३०] at कान्ची, having शन्ख, Cakra, अक्षवलय, and Pustaka (book) in his hand;
2: Br. IV. 5. 9, ३५-40.
resides in Sutalam.
3: Ib. II. २०. २१; वा. ५०. २०.

--see अश्वमेध and वाजिमेध;
1: Br. III. ४७. ४५, ४७.
of ब्रह्मा over the गयाशीला; विष्णु and other Gods promised to occupy the शिला for मोक्ष of the पितृ;
2: वा. १०८. 9-१०.
of दक्ष, ruined;
3: Ib. ३०. ७९, ११०.
